      "summary": "This review examined teaching intended to improve reading comprehension in autistic students. It searched literature published from 2000 to 2019 and included 25 studies. The authors reported that students could benefit from targeted instruction. Common targets included making inferences and identifying a text's main idea; direct instruction was frequently used. However, the review also identified incomplete descriptions of the particular comprehension processes being taught. The findings support choosing a concrete comprehension goal rather than assuming that accurate word reading means a child understands the message. For parents and teachers, short meaningful captions and discussion can be useful practice opportunities when adapted to the learner. The abstract does not establish which approach is best for an individual child, and the review does not validate this app, picture-choice tasks or a particular digital course sequence.",
