      "summary": "This review considered interventions for preschool and primary-school children with developmental language disorder, up to eight years of age. It included 27 studies and examined several different language domains. The authors found support for some phonological interventions and some expressive grammar work, while evidence for other outcomes was limited or inconsistent. Results for one language domain should therefore not be assumed to apply to all receptive and expressive skills. A useful practical approach is to identify a specific difficulty, model the relevant language and observe whether learning appears beyond the practice task. Matching familiar pictures is not equivalent to improving receptive vocabulary or treating a language disorder. The abstract gives an overview, but does not permit a full appraisal of each intervention's quality, intensity or suitability. A relevant professional should help interpret teaching needs where difficulties persist.",
